 "text": "On the night of November twenty-eighth it was held by a single understrength Marine battalion under Lieutenant Colonel Thomas Ridge. He had only a few thousand men to defend a perimeter about four miles around. Truck drivers and engineers and clerks were handed rifles and sent to the line.",
